From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:36:05 -0644
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: gs201-cp: turn the sleep guard on for zumapro

The system sleep handling for the modem's link (the refusal while the
link is up, before the freeze and again at noirq; the root port and the
endpoint kept out of the PCI core's sleep path) is behind sleep_guard,
and only gs201 sets it. zumapro has the same link driver and CPIF and
fails the same way without it: a system sleep with the modem's link
down puts the root port in D3hot with the device inaccessible, the
resume waits for a link that isn't coming, and CPIF reads 0xffff from
the modem's command register until a reboot.

Set sleep_guard for zumapro, and say so where the comments name gs201
alone.

Tested on a Pixel 9a (tegu) with the modem registered on LTE with IMS
voice and SMS, Wi-Fi connected and the cellular data service running:

- with the series as it was under review plus the maintainer's two
  review patches (the second a ring trace, left out of the merge): 300
  sleep requests of 60 s in one boot, 299 entered and woke (239 on the
  RTC alarm, 60 on cp2ap_wakeup) and 1 refused before the freeze with
  the link up; after every one the CP was ONLINE and the phone service
  answered. Calls and texts sent to the sleeping palmtop woke it on
  cp2ap_wakeup, and rang or arrived;
- with the series as merged: 10 sleeps entered, none refused or failed,
  in a boot of 954 link power-ups.

In those boots there was no "Unable to change power state", "Link
Active not set", "Can't set D0", "BME" or UFS error handler line, and
the shutdowns stopped the modem cleanly. Without the guard the same
phone lost the modem at the first sleep with the link down.

One open point from the same testing, not on the sleep path: a boot of
the first build hung once at a link power-up while awake, before the
PHY's external PLL lock was reported (the 1,549th power-up of that
boot); none in over 15,000 power-ups since, on either build.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c
index 7ed4650b2..1677a2346 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-gs201-cp.c
@@ -248,8 +248,8 @@ static const char * const cp_input_names[CP_NUM_INPUTS] = {
  * @sysreg_optional: without samsung,sysreg the link runs without I/O
  *	coherency
  * @sleep_guard: system sleep with the modem up has been tried on this SoC
- *	(gs201): the noirq sleep callbacks run, and the root port is kept out
- *	of the PCI core's D3 handling; elsewhere neither happens
+ *	(gs201, zumapro): the noirq sleep callbacks run, and the root port is
+ *	kept out of the PCI core's D3 handling; elsewhere neither happens
  */
 struct gs201_pcie_cp_data {
 	bool zuma_ctrl;
@@ -865,7 +865,7 @@ static int cp_bus(struct gs201_pcie_cp *cp)
 	 * read back all ones. Its windows are this driver's, restored at
 	 * every link up (cp_root_win_restore()).
 	 * All of this only where system sleep with the modem up has been
-	 * tried (sleep_guard, gs201).
+	 * tried (sleep_guard: gs201, zumapro).
 	 */
 	if (cp->data->sleep_guard) {
 		list_for_each_entry(rp, &cp->bridge->bus->devices, bus_list) {
@@ -2397,7 +2397,8 @@ static void gs201_pcie_cp_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 }
 
 /*
- * System sleep (s2idle) with the modem up, on gs201 only (sleep_guard).
+ * System sleep (s2idle) with the modem up, on gs201 and zumapro only
+ * (sleep_guard).
  * The modem stays powered; its driver lets the AP sleep only once
  * CP2AP_WAKEUP has dropped and the idle link has been powered down (cpif
  * holds a wake lock while the link is up, and its suspend refuses while
@@ -2470,6 +2471,7 @@ static const struct gs201_pcie_cp_data zumapro_pcie_cp_data = {
 	.phy_bypass_once = true,
 	.host_atu = true,
 	.sysreg_optional = true,
+	.sleep_guard = true,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id gs201_pcie_cp_of_match[] = {
